foundation.solution_text:
1. **Find the dot product of the two vectors**
$\underset{\sim}{a}\cdot\underset{\sim}{b} = (-5)(3)+(1)(4)$
$= -11$
2. **Find the square of the magnitude of the vector being projected onto**
$|\underset{\sim}{b}|^{2} = 3^2+4^2 = 25$
3. **Divide the dot product by this squared magnitude, then multiply by the vector being projected onto**
$\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a} = -\dfrac{11}{25}\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$
$= \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{33}{25} \\ -\frac{44}{25} \end{pmatrix}$
The scalar is negative, so the shadow points the opposite way to $\underset{\sim}{b}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.75cm, y=0.75cm]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta, calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-5,1);
\coordinate (B) at (3,4);
\coordinate (P) at (-1.32,-1.76);
\draw[dashed, gray] (-2.4,-3.2) -- (O);
\draw[-{Stealth[length=3mm]}] (O) -- (B) node[pos=1, above right] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\draw[-{Stealth[length=3mm]}] (O) -- (A) node[pos=1, left] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[thick, -{Stealth[length=3mm]}] (O) -- (P) node[pos=1, below right] {$\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[dashed] (A) -- (P);
\coordinate (p1) at ($(P)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (p2) at ($(P)!0.3cm!(O)$);
\draw (p1) -- ($(p1)+(p2)-(P)$) -- (p2);
